.TH BANDCAMP_DL_RB 1 "2026-09-11" "bandcamp-dl-rb 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bandcamp_dl_rb \- download your Bandcamp purchases into a Plex-friendly
music library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bandcamp_dl_rb
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIbandcamp-username\fR
.br
.B bandcamp_dl_rb
[\fIoptions\fR] \fB\-\-url\fR \fIurl\fR ...
.br
.B bandcamp_dl_rb
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
.B bandcamp_dl_rb
\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bandcamp_dl_rb
authenticates to Bandcamp with your browser session cookie, scans your
collection, and downloads each purchase as FLAC (or the best available format)
into a clean
.IR Artist / Album / track
layout.
.PP
Provide your Bandcamp username to sync your whole collection, or pass specific
album or track page URLs with
.B \-\-url,
item IDs with
.B \-\-items,
or a regex with
.B \-\-filter
to download exactly what you want.
.PP
A small state file,
.BR .bandcamp\-sync.json ,
is written into the library after each run so subsequent runs skip albums that
are already present.
.PP
To find your username, visit bandcamp.com and look at your profile URL; it ends
in your username (for example
.IR https://bandcamp.com/yourname ).
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The official Bandcamp API is only for labels and merch partners, so this tool
uses the same undocumented /api/fancollection/* endpoints the website does,
authenticated with your session
.B identity
cookie.
.IP \(bu 4
The script extracts the cookie automatically from Firefox, then Safari (macOS
only), then Chrome or Chromium. Use
.B \-\-browser
to force a specific browser.
.IP \(bu 4
If automatic extraction fails, export a Netscape-format cookies.txt with a
browser extension and pass the file with
.B \-\-cookie-file,
or paste the raw
.B identity
cookie value found in DevTools (F12) \(-> Application \(-> Cookies \(->
bandcamp.com.
.PP
The
.B identity
cookie is a full-session credential; treat it like a password. Do not commit
it, share it, or leave it in shell history.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Authentication
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cookie-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a Netscape-format cookies.txt file, or a raw
.B identity
cookie value.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-browser " " \fIBROWSER\fR
Browser to extract cookies from:
.BR firefox ", " chrome ", " chromium ", " safari ", or " auto
(default:
.BR auto ,
which tries Firefox, then Safari, then Chrome; Safari is macOS-only).
.SS Library and formats
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-library " " \fIPATH\fR
Plex library root path; required. Albums are written to
.IR PATH / Artist / Album .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Audio format to download (default:
.BR flac ).
If the exact format is unavailable, the script falls back through the quality
ladder described in
.BR FORMATS "."
.SS What to download
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Download a specific album or track by its Bandcamp page URL. Repeatable. The
script finds the item in your collection and reports it as not found (and
moves on) if it is not owned by your account.
.TP
.BR \-\-items " " \fIIDS\fR
Download specific collection items by ID, for example
.BR a100,t200 .
Requires the username argument. IDs appear in
.B \-\-dry-run
output as
.RI [a100]
.I Artist\~\-~\~Album .
.TP
.BR \-\-filter " " \fIREGEX\fR
Download only collection items whose artist or title matches the given regex
(case-insensitive). Requires the username argument. The regex is matched
against
.IR "artist title" ,
so it can match both fields, e.g.
.BR 'radiohead.*amnesiac' .
An invalid regex, or one that matches nothing, exits non-zero and downloads
nothing.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-include-hidden
Also download items hidden in your collection.
.TP
.BR \-\-since " " \fIDATE\fR
Only items purchased on or after
.IR YYYY-MM-DD .
.TP
.BR \-\-until " " \fIDATE\fR
Only items purchased before
.IR YYYY-MM-DD .
.SS Behavior
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
Download up to
.I N
albums in parallel (1-4, default:
.BR 1 ).
Keep
.I N
small; Bandcamp throttles session endpoints.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Re-download even if the album already exists, and refresh the
.B album.json
sidecar.
.TP
.B \-\-no-unzip
Save album downloads as ZIP archives (named after the album) instead of
extracting track files.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
List what would be downloaded, with item IDs and sizes, without downloading
anything.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.SS Help and version
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FORMATS
Supported formats:
.PP
.nf
flac   mp3-320   mp3-v0   wav   aiff-lossless   aac-hi   alac   vorbis
.fi
.PP
When the requested format is not available, the script falls back through this
quality order:
.PP
.nf
flac \(-> wav \(-> aiff-lossless \(-> alac \(-> aac-hi \(-> mp3-320 \(-> mp3-v0 \(-> vorbis
.fi
.PP
If nothing is available, the album is reported as unavailable and skipped.
.SH EXAMPLES
Download the whole collection as FLAC:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bandcamp_dl_rb --library ~/Music/Bandcamp yourname
.RE
.fi
.PP
Only purchases since a date, as WAV:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bandcamp_dl_rb -l ~/Music/Bandcamp --since 2025-01-01 -f wav yourname
.RE
.fi
.PP
Download specific albums or tracks by URL:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bandcamp_dl_rb -l ~/Music/Bandcamp \\
    --url https://radiohead.bandcamp.com/album/in-rainbows \\
    --url https://aphextwin.bandcamp.com/track/windowlicker yourname
.RE
.fi
.PP
Preview the run without downloading:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bandcamp_dl_rb -l ~/Music/Bandcamp --dry-run yourname
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a manual cookie file:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
bandcamp_dl_rb -l ~/Music/Bandcamp --cookie-file /path/to/cookies.txt yourname
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Music/Bandcamp/.bandcamp-sync.json
State file written after each run; used to skip already-downloaded albums.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. Also returned by
.B \-\-help
and
.BR \-\-version .
.TP
.B 1
Failure: invalid arguments, no identity cookie found, no downloadable items
found, or one or more downloads failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full documentation, including detailed notes on Firefox, Safari, Chrome,
and manual cookie extraction, is available in the project README:
.PP
.RS 4
https://github.com/alexcoll/bandcamp-dl-rb
.RE
.PP
Shell completion files for bash, zsh, and fish ship with the gem in the
.I completions
directory.
.SH CAVEATS
This tool uses undocumented, unsupported Bandcamp endpoints that may change at
any time. It is intended for downloading music you have already paid for into a
personal, locally backed library.